WEBVTT

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.980
And give her a teaspoon of the medicine after every meal.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:13.800
Don't worry. She'll be fine.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.140
How are you?

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.830
I'm tired and hungry.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.230
Well, Marilyn and Richard called.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.880
They'll be here soon, and then we'll eat.

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:41.850
Well, she'll be here later.

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.000
She has to work late tonight.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.060
And what's Robbie cooking for dinner?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.780
It's a surprise.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.140
I hope it's pasta.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.340
Robbie, the dinner was terrific.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.460
Yes, it was delicious.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.780
What's for dessert?

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:05.080
Don't worry.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:07.380
We've got lots of ice cream.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.880
Oh, I'd love some ice cream.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:15.230
Well, there's chocolate and coffee and a little vanilla.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:17.940
Is that all right with everyone?

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:19.440
I'll have chocolate.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.220
Me, too.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.280
and one scoop of chocolate for me.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.000
Robbie, will you help me serve?

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.890
I keep thinking about that bag of film. Eight rolls.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.440
A whole day's work.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:49.500
And good stuff, too.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.000
Don't worry, Richard.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:04.240
I'll get it. Hello.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:05.380
Hello.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.540
Does Richard Stewart live here?

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.040
Yes, he's my brother.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.520
I'm Robbie...Robbie Stewart.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.800
I'm Alexandra Pappas.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:15.720
How do you do?

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:20.380
Your brother left his bag of film on the ferryboat.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:21.420
I found it.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:23.320
I'm really glad to see you.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.600
I mean...my brother'll be really glad to see you!

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.560
Robbie! Who is it?

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:30.760
It's Richard's film!

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.520
I mean, Alexandra Pappas.

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:36.040
Come in, please.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.320
Hello, Richard. I found your bag!

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.520
Oh, thank you! Thank you!

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:52.460
This is my wife Marilyn.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.240
Richard showed me your photo.

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.600
How do you do?

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:56.520
Oh yes.

00:02:56.580 --> 00:02:58.170
Richard told us all about you.

00:02:58.170 --> 00:02:59.300
It's nice to meet you.

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.300
And this is my mother, Ellen Stewart.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:02.380
How do you do?

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.680
And my father, Dr. Philip Stewart.

00:03:05.030 --> 00:03:06.280
Nice to meet you, Alexandra.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.320
Yes. And you must be Susan. Hi.

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:12.620
Hi. Welcome.

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.830
I'm so glad you found the bag

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:16.920
and took the time and trouble to return it.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.120
Oh, it was no trouble.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.280
I just took the wrong train.

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.190
Would you like something to eat?

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:23.280
Thank you, no.

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.440
I'm late for dinner at my house.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:26.620
I really have to go.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:28.080
Would you like to call home?

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:29.780
I'd appreciate that.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:31.660
Please, use the phone.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:33.220
Thanks. Excuse me.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:36.780
Alexandra's a high-school exchange student from Greece.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.160
Where does she live?

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:39.910
With a family in the Bronx.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.300
Oh, that's not too far from here!

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:43.740
Take it easy, Robbie.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.180
Thank you.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.200
I can only stay a few minutes.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:52.780
Thanks, Mrs. Stewart.

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.580
Please sit down, Alexandra.

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:03.840
So, you're an exchange student.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:05.440
Where do you go to school?

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.420
At the Bronx High School of Science.

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.700
Oh, that's a very good school.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.720
What are your favorite subjects?

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.000
Biology and mathematics.

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.200
Richard tells me you're a doctor.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.380
Yes, a pediatrician.

00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:20.980
And what does your father do?

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.300
He's a lawyer, in Thessaloniki.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.100
Would you like some pasta?

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:26.100
I made it myself.

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.040
It might be a little cold.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.480
Thanks, no. I do have to go.

00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.680
It was nice meeting you all.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:37.200
Well, maybe you'll come for lunch some Sunday,

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.400
so we can really thank you

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.900
for bringing Richard's bag back.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:40.360
Maybe.

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:42.680
You're welcome anytime.

00:04:42.790 --> 00:04:43.550
Good-bye.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.480
Can I drive you home?

00:04:51.700 --> 00:04:52.600
No, thanks.

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:53.980
The train is just up the street.

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.220
It won't take me long at all.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:04:59.200
Bye.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:04:59.980
Bye-bye.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:00.620
Good night.

00:05:09.640 --> 00:05:12.900
She's a smart young lady, and very nice.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:16.680
Very! Hey, she forgot her bag!

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:19.840
I guess we'll be seeing Alexandra again.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:20.820
Right, Robbie?
